               <birth when="1764-11-06"><placeName>New Galloway, Kirkcudbrightshire</placeName></birth>
               <death when="1807-04-13"><placeName>London, England</placeName></death>
               <occupation>Writer</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>Robert Heron was a Scottish writer who moved to London in 1799 and was the Editor of Globe, British press and a parliamentary reporter. In 1806 he founded a newspaper called The Fame, which was unsuccessful. After spending time in Newgate prison for debt, he fell ill and died in St Pancras Hospital. </p>
